     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of about 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day divided twice daily.** That is 850 mg PO BID with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO BID with meals.** These are common standard regimens.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose."
      }
     ],
