       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and the reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for exceeding it. I don't know of any indication that supports this dose in a patient with normal renal and hepatic function. It risks serious harm, including lactic acidosis, and extra drug won't improve glycemic control past the labeled maximum.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals.** This is the maximum labeled dose, 2,550 mg/day.\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO BID with meals.**\n- **A lower starting dose with titration.** For example, 500 mg PO BID with meals, increased over 1\u20132 weeks as tolerated.\n\nIf you think this patient needs an off-label dose, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy or the clinical pharmacist first. They can document the rationale and approve the order through your hospital's override process. Tell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
